  "description": "<p>This bug is seen when trying to create a basic container with a \"charset\" included in the \"Content-Type\" header.</p>\n\n<p>For example, the following execution returns successfully:<br/>\n$ curl -i -X PUT localhost:8080/rest/test -H'Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer</a>&gt;; rel=\"type\"' -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle\" -d \"&lt;&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://example.com/title\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://example.com/title</a>&gt; 'Hello'\"</p>\n\n<p>However, by adding the charset parameter to the Content-Type, we get a 500 response:<br/>\ncurl -i -X PUT localhost:8080/rest/test -H'Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer</a>&gt;; rel=\"type\"' -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle; charset=ISO-8859-1\" -d \"&lt;&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://example.com/title\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://example.com/title</a>&gt; 'Hello'\"</p>",
